WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:04.020
Hey, this is going to bring great pleasure
to many in our audience.

00:00:04.020 --> 00:00:06.170
It's time to say bye bye to me.

00:00:06.170 --> 00:00:12.170
David Packman is leaving the David Pakman
show just for four shows next week.

00:00:12.170 --> 00:00:15.420
Next week we're going to be having guests
hosts Monday through Thursday.

00:00:15.420 --> 00:00:22.269
And then we are sort of wrapping the Memorial
Day holiday, uh, to include next Friday so

00:00:22.269 --> 00:00:27.690
that staff gets a, an additional day off in
addition to, uh, the federal holiday.

00:00:27.690 --> 00:00:31.260
So we're going to be having guests hosts for
the first, first part of next week, Ben Dickson.

00:00:31.260 --> 00:00:36.900
We'll be splitting guest hosting duties with
Farron cousins from ring of fire.

00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:42.170
Uh, I'm going to be combining my much overdue
vacation, which I skipped.

00:00:42.170 --> 00:00:43.220
People may not know this.

00:00:43.220 --> 00:00:49.760
Um, I, I martyred myself so that everybody
else could get a vacation early in 2019 and

00:00:49.760 --> 00:00:54.580
I skipped mine and I am now going to be taking
a few days off combining it with a trip to

00:00:54.580 --> 00:00:58.340
a wedding and, uh, sort of a, a work trip.

00:00:58.340 --> 00:01:00.830
Um, and then we'll have the memorial day holiday.

00:01:00.830 --> 00:01:04.989
So people who want me kicked off of my own
show, which shockingly is a bigger number

00:01:04.989 --> 00:01:06.479
than you might imagine.

00:01:06.479 --> 00:01:10.880
I effectively am being kicked off of my own
show for all of next week and you'll have

00:01:10.880 --> 00:01:11.880
a week break.

00:01:11.880 --> 00:01:16.360
Although I never really understood if you
dislike me that much, if you dislike this

00:01:16.360 --> 00:01:20.950
program that much, it seems like you could
just watch a different show or listen to a

00:01:20.950 --> 00:01:25.560
different podcast or just if you listen on
the radio tune to something else.

00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:28.399
But it seems like for a lot of people that's
not a possibility.

00:01:28.399 --> 00:01:30.759
They want to be listening to this show.

00:01:30.759 --> 00:01:34.619
They just want someone else hosting it, which
doesn't really make sense when it's the David

00:01:34.619 --> 00:01:35.619
Pakman show.

00:01:35.619 --> 00:01:36.619
I don't know.

00:01:36.619 --> 00:01:37.619
But I will be back.

00:01:37.619 --> 00:01:39.310
Uh, please be nice to Faron.

00:01:39.310 --> 00:01:42.490
Uh, and to Ben, they're going to do a really,
really great job.

00:01:42.490 --> 00:01:44.049
They're going to do the regular show.

00:01:44.049 --> 00:01:47.290
They're going to do the bonus show for our
members and our patrons.

00:01:47.290 --> 00:01:50.829
Uh, and remember that thanks to your support.

00:01:50.829 --> 00:01:56.789
We now have the staffing and resources that
we can rotate, break.

00:01:56.789 --> 00:02:00.329
So instead of everybody just having to go
on break at the same time, and the show is

00:02:00.329 --> 00:02:06.259
just dark for periods, including up to sometimes
two weeks of shows, uh, we still have production

00:02:06.259 --> 00:02:11.349
staff when I'm away, and then I come back
and we have rotating production staff and

00:02:11.349 --> 00:02:13.090
we can afford to bring in the guest host.

00:02:13.090 --> 00:02:18.041
So this is all because of your support over
the last, um, I guess over the last year and

00:02:18.041 --> 00:02:21.189
a half to two years, we've really, really
been able to ramp this up.

00:02:21.189 --> 00:02:22.580
Uh, so thank you.

00:02:22.580 --> 00:02:27.680
Uh, consider participating in that funding
of progressive independent media by grabbing

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:36.700
